<section class="eg-section eg-section-tint" id="node-contract">
  <div class="eg-container eg-split">
    <div>
      <span class="eg-eyebrow">The LlmNode contract</span><h2>A stage you can read in one place.</h2>
      <p class="eg-lede">The node says what the model should do. Its handler says what the application will accept.</p>
      <ol class="eg-contract-list">
        <li><b>01</b><div><strong>Declare the prompt and allowed tools.</strong><p>The city collector offers <code>capture_city</code>, with a schema checked before its handler runs.</p></div></li>
        <li><b>02</b><div><strong>Save facts where they become valid.</strong><p><code>saveState()</code> stages a write to the current node's typed channel. Shared context has an explicit home too.</p></div></li>
        <li><b>03</b><div><strong>Return an explicit outcome.</strong><p><code>stay()</code> supplies corrective tool feedback; <code>go()</code> enters the next stage. Replies and completion have their own builders.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/developer-guide/nodes-and-execution/">Read the lifecycle and execution contract <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="eg-code"><div class="eg-code-head"><span>CityNode · abridged from the starter</span><span>TypeScript</span></div><pre><code class="language-typescript">class CityNode extends LlmNode&lt;StarterStateType&gt; {
  getPrompt() {
    return "Ask for a city, then call capture_city.";
  }

  defineTool(): readonly ToolDefinition[] {
    return [{
      name: "capture_city",
      description: "Save a destination city.",
      schema: z.object({ city: z.string().min(2) }),
    }];
  }

  @Tool("capture_city")
  async captureCity({ city }: { city: string }) {
    const value = city.trim();
    if (!/^[\p{L} .'-]+$/u.test(value)) {
      return stay("Ask for a valid city name.");
    }
    this.saveState({ city: value });
    return go(SummaryNode);
  }
}</code></pre></div>
  </div>
</section>
